--- !u!114 &8749121131333605047
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 4423815028851150653}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: a6c638bf07f19cc428b27368804fb218, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::QuestFlight.Product.Training.TrainingCoach
  training: {fileID: 406945266046702129}
  flight: {fileID: 742791276885309778}
  instrumentProvider: {fileID: 4122695829926210968}
  lines:
  - cue: 1
    reference: 2
    text: The right bank is too steep. Ease the yoke left to reduce it.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: c476b69c83895d340b2b741962ae0a4d, type: 3}
  - cue: 2
    reference: 2
    text: The left bank is too steep. Ease the yoke right to reduce it.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 1ef5e4e4f050b8b44bbfe5669ff390cd, type: 3}
  - cue: 3
    reference: 0
    text: Approaching the target heading. Begin rolling left to wings level.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 95cf4b3861cb78e488d5e96feebdb672, type: 3}
  - cue: 4
    reference: 0
    text: Approaching the target heading. Begin rolling right to wings level.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: bd89871be00f7fe41a4c4a3b9d91d73e, type: 3}
  - cue: 5
    reference: 4
    text: The target is to your left. Begin a gentle left turn.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: a4815dacfcc1b6841af43f66d44cb0fc, type: 3}
  - cue: 6
    reference: 4
    text: The target is to your right. Begin a gentle right turn.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 1e46bca7e70ce4746b2702018392cedf, type: 3}
  - cue: 7
    reference: 3
    text: You are below the target altitude. Check attitude and power; establish
      a gentle climb if airspeed permits.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: d74bd4937aef21f44a5622dfa5bcaa16, type: 3}
  - cue: 8
    reference: 3
    text: You are above the target altitude. Ease toward a gentle descent and monitor
      airspeed.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: d87b3c622fd9fe94c84535e8354c3cb5, type: 3}
  - cue: 9
    reference: 1
    text: Airspeed is low. Check nose attitude and power before continuing the maneuver.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 1e8b73060832fca468448c2b5d46d88f, type: 3}
  - cue: 10
    reference: 1
    text: Airspeed is high. Check power and your descent attitude; make a small correction.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 2b6c4d73c04d8ab409f8ca5aa4e1ce93, type: 3}
  - cue: 11
    reference: 6
    text: The ball is left of center. Add a little left rudder, then ease it as the
      ball centers.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: d256d82ca81fdb8408b9bdf9ad1f2a1b, type: 3}
  - cue: 12
    reference: 6
    text: The ball is right of center. Add a little right rudder, then ease it as
      the ball centers.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: df46ee5f4a499614b8f1b195f7d1a5d2, type: 3}
  - cue: 13
    reference: 7
    text: Taxi speed is too high. Reduce power and brake gently back to walking speed.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 52c3ec557f55493419e44fbbebedee08, type: 3}
  - cue: 14
    reference: 11
    text: Throttle idle. Apply both brakes and stop before the runway.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 3be499465c93d8c4c8ae072099042681, type: 3}
  - cue: 15
    reference: 7
    text: Increase power smoothly for this phase. Keep monitoring airspeed and direction.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: c4dc57bd20635ad409484d3cb290267f, type: 3}
  - cue: 16
    reference: 0
    text: Squeeze both index triggers to apply both brakes. Keep throttle at idle.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 479d931d1e0408f4b90d47409ab15429, type: 3}
  - cue: 17
    reference: 8
    text: Grip the yoke and move it through the requested directions, then center
      it.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 02a99d6b83e2dac4796fdf839a891d86, type: 3}
  - cue: 18
    reference: 6
    text: Use the right thumbstick for rudder. Move it both ways, then center it.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: c89d54e60b3e70d4ebb298f1af6101e3, type: 3}
  - cue: 19
    reference: 10
    text: Use small left-thumbstick inputs to trim until less yoke input is needed.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 4d474dac387988348b43c7366a1a89d3, type: 3}
  - cue: 20
    reference: 9
    text: Positive climb established. Reduce flaps to the next instructed setting.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: daacfe6c95db6da4aaa3af4eb888f2ab, type: 3}
  - cue: 21
    reference: 11
    text: Check runway alignment. Use a gentle correction; go around if a safe alignment
      is not possible.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 9bc12a652bf2b31429be1cf87f5bdfa8, type: 3}
  - cue: 23
    reference: 7
    text: 'Unstable approach. Go around: full power, establish the climb, then retract
      flaps in stages.'
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 8feb4558b18b64145b6a9b8f93f16183, type: 3}
  - cue: 24
    reference: 0
    text: That correction is working. Let the aircraft settle and look outside.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 43fbc5e901d14e4439061a55395fa781, type: 3}
  markers:
  - reference: 0
    marker: {fileID: 0}
    explanation: Look through the windshield. Use the distant horizon to judge aircraft
      attitude, and keep scanning for traffic. Cross-check instruments briefly, then
      look outside again.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: e52158c0a5ff9cc40bcffe865cdda850, type: 3}
  - reference: 2
    marker: {fileID: 4425453207326071263}
    explanation: The attitude indicator shows the airplane against a small artificial
      horizon. Compare it with the real horizon; avoid staring at the instrument.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 7653e712d7115f74f9032faf28cf8160, type: 3}
  - reference: 1
    marker: {fileID: 5092024740439860943}
    explanation: This is the airspeed indicator. Read the needle against the knots
      scale. Ninety knots is the level-flight target for this exercise.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: aff7196ea0dc7d04283a2c4b8b929121, type: 3}
  - reference: 3
    marker: {fileID: 4000679654135065730}
    explanation: This is the altimeter. Its numeric reading and hands show indicated
      altitude in feet. The level-flight target is seven thousand feet.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 57fae532dfbf490468dc197f2aac8579, type: 3}
  - reference: 4
    marker: {fileID: 787841819118726404}
    explanation: Read heading at the top index. Nine means zero nine zero degrees.
      This simulator's heading indicator uses true heading; use this dial for lesson
      targets, not the magnetic compass.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 9a299125aa342b642a10fbc55b79b68b, type: 3}
  - reference: 5
    marker: {fileID: 4439288029712437313}
    explanation: This needle shows climbing or descending in feet per minute. Use
      it to confirm a trend; make small attitude corrections and allow the indication
      to settle.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: a3225b1be009755499b61aa79b3f7e18, type: 3}
  - reference: 6
    marker: {fileID: 1206341969298665581}
    explanation: The ball shows coordination. Use gentle rudder toward the displaced
      ball, then ease the input as it centers. The right thumbstick controls rudder.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 1e6be9d8ba9364b46837a5c139205555, type: 3}
  - reference: 7
    marker: {fileID: 4304181155796354961}
    explanation: Grip the throttle knob to adjust power. Add or reduce power smoothly,
      then check how airspeed and climb change.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 10afa75edbca51443baae86ab85b10d2, type: 3}
  - reference: 8
    marker: {fileID: 4300490960307867227}
    explanation: Grip the yoke. Left and right inputs roll the airplane; forward
      and back inputs change pitch. Release the correcting input as the desired attitude
      is reached.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: a678192489542734b9293c22a37495dc, type: 3}
  - reference: 9
    marker: {fileID: 5864090527383306501}
    explanation: Use the flap selector to choose a position. Confirm the flap indication
      and keep within the taught airspeed range before extending flaps.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 803aa3af0648a7b4696aba5e1eab0106, type: 3}
  - reference: 10
    marker: {fileID: 0}
    explanation: The left thumbstick adjusts trim during manual flight. Use small
      up or down inputs to reduce the yoke input needed to hold attitude. There is
      no force feedback.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 11493793927912346a949ba47c0e089f, type: 3}
  - reference: 11
    marker: {fileID: 0}
    explanation: Identify runway zero eight and its paved edges outside. The north-side
      pattern keeps the runway to your left. For taxi, stay on the taxiway and stop
      before entering the runway.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 3629e726067530844bc4730779ff57a7, type: 3}
  worldMarker: {fileID: 3661077398707941412}
  worldMarkerPulse: {fileID: 2501880960978424173}
